findings.proposal:
Create @utility recipes in utilities.css:
```css
@utility collapse-animate {
  @apply transition-[height,opacity] duration-[var(--duration-normal)] ease-[var(--ease-standard)];
}
@utility carousel-dot-animate {
  @apply transition-[background-color,transform,width,height,box-shadow] duration-[var(--duration-fast)] ease-[var(--ease-standard)];
}
```
Then use `collapse-animate` instead of embedding properties per-component. Reduces redundancy and improves debuggability.

Lift these chains to @layer components rules in utilities.css:
```css
@layer components {
  .command-dialog-heading {
    @apply px-2 font-medium text-muted-foreground;
  }
}
```
Then use `[&_[cmdk-group-heading]]:command-dialog-heading` or simpler: scope the component wrapper with a class that applies these rules to its descendants. Alternatively, inline the styles in the CommandDialog/CommandGroup component wrapper rather than spreading across children.

For locally controlled vars like --carousel-nav-size, add to @theme and use standard utilities. For reka-ui injected vars, create documented @utility wrappers:
```css
@utility carousel-nav-size {
  @apply h-[var(--carousel-nav-size)] w-[var(--carousel-nav-size)];
}
```
Rename to `carousel-nav-size` and apply to CarouselNext/CarouselPrevious. For reka-ui runtime-injected vars, accept the arbitrary-value pattern but document why (external API).

For the dialog width pattern, add a token:
```css
--size-modal-inner-width: calc(100% - 2rem);
```
Then expose via @theme and use `w-modal-inner`. For carousel nav positioning, create a @utility:
```css
@utility carousel-nav-negative-offset {
  @apply left-[calc(-1*var(--carousel-nav-offset))];
}
```
Or better: simplify by moving positioning logic to a CSS rule on `.carousel-next` / `.carousel-prev` element.

Extract to @utility recipes (6 total):
```css
@utility stack-overlap-sm { @apply -mt-[var(--stack-overlap-sm)]; }
@utility stack-overlap-md { @apply -mt-[var(--stack-overlap-md)]; }
@utility stack-overlap-lg { @apply -mt-[var(--stack-overlap-lg)]; }
@utility stack-overlap-horizontal-sm { @apply -ml-[var(--stack-overlap-sm)]; }
/* ... etc */
```
Or simpler: inline these as computed class bindings in the component's `overlapClass` computed property, updating StackedIconGroup to emit `stack-overlap-sm` type names and bind via a utility map.

Add all motion tokens to @theme block in theme.css (currently @theme has `--duration-fast` etc. but they need to be explicitly exposed as Tailwind `duration-*` utilities). Example:
```css
@theme {
  --duration-fast: var(--duration-fast);
  --duration-normal: var(--duration-normal);
  /* ... */
}
```
Then use `duration-fast` instead of `duration-[var(--duration-fast)]`. For easings, add to @theme and use `animation-*` or custom easing utilities via `ease-*` naming.
